      "page_title": "Rebase vs Merge",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Are They?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Merge== joins two histories with a new commit that has two parents",
            "History stays a true DAG, showing where the branch diverged",
            "==Rebase== replays your commits on top of another base",
            "Result is a linear history with no merge commit",
            "Rebase makes **NEW** commits with new SHAs; old ones live until gc"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Merge vs Rebase",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Merge",
            "Rebase"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Extra commit",
              "merge commit, 2 parents",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "History shape",
              "branching DAG",
              "straight line"
            ],
            [
              "SHAs",
              "unchanged",
              "**new** SHAs"
            ],
            [
              "Preserves",
              "context (when it diverged)",
              "readability"
            ],
            [
              "Safety",
              "non-destructive",
              "rewrites history"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Trade-off",
          "text": "Rebase is not a replacement for merge. Pick by what you need."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Fast-Forward",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Target has no new commits: merge just moves the pointer",
            "No merge commit is created",
            "`--no-ff` forces a merge commit even when ff is possible"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git merge feature          # ff if able",
            "git merge --no-ff feature  # always commit"
          ],
          "note": "--no-ff keeps the branch visible"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Worked Example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git switch feature",
            "git rebase main     # after main's tip",
            "git switch main",
            "git merge feature  # fast-forward"
          ],
          "note": "rebase first, then ff merge"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "A",
              "B",
              "C",
              "D'",
              "E'"
            ],
            "indices": false,
            "pointers": [
              {
                "index": 2,
                "label": "main",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "index": 4,
                "label": "feature",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ],
            "highlight": [
              3,
              4
            ],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "D', E' are replayed copies: a clean line"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Pulling Changes",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default `git pull` = fetch + **merge**",
            "`git pull --rebase` = fetch + **rebase** instead",
            "`pull.rebase=true` makes rebase the default pull"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git pull --rebase",
            "git config pull.rebase true"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of Thumb",
          "text": "Rebase to tidy your own local work. Merge to integrate shared work."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Two ways to integrate"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "How Commits Are Replayed",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What a commit is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A commit is a ==snapshot== plus a **parent** pointer, author and message. Change the parent and the __SHA__ changes too.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tree",
              "the snapshot"
            ],
            [
              "parent",
              "previous commit"
            ],
            [
              "author",
              "who wrote it"
            ],
            [
              "message",
              "why it exists"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The 5 replay steps",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Find the ==merge-base== of branch and upstream",
            "Collect `upstream..HEAD`: reachable from HEAD, not upstream",
            "Detach HEAD, checkout the **upstream** tip",
            "`cherry-pick` each commit, a three-way merge",
            "Move branch name to the last new commit, drop old pointer"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git switch feature",
            "git rebase main",
            "# 1 base = merge-base main HEAD",
            "# 2 list = main..HEAD",
            "# 3-5 replay, then move branch"
          ],
          "note": "Old tip stays until gc"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: A B C on main",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "M",
              "X",
              "Y",
              "A'",
              "B'",
              "C'"
            ],
            "indices": false,
            "pointers": [
              {
                "index": 0,
                "label": "old base",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "index": 2,
                "label": "main tip",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "index": 5,
                "label": "feature",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ],
            "highlight": [
              3,
              4,
              5
            ],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "A B C replayed after Y, main's tip: new SHAs"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Commit",
            "Author",
            "Date",
            "SHA"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "A",
              "kept",
              "new",
              "new"
            ],
            [
              "B",
              "kept",
              "new",
              "new"
            ],
            [
              "C",
              "kept",
              "new",
              "new"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Author and message are kept, committer date is new",
            "Child hash includes parent hash, so ==descendants== all change",
            "Same ==patch-id== already upstream? Skipped automatically"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git range-diff main..ORIG_HEAD \\",
            "  main..HEAD",
            "git reset --hard ORIG_HEAD",
            "ls .git/rebase-merge/"
          ],
          "note": "range-diff compares old and new"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "State of a rebase",
          "text": "HEAD is detached mid-rebase. ORIG_HEAD holds the old tip. State lives in .git/rebase-merge/."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Thinking rebase moves commits; it **copies** them",
            "Quoting an old SHA after rebase; it is stale",
            "Panicking at detached HEAD; it is normal mid-rebase",
            "Not checking `range-diff`, so changes slip in unseen"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Five-step replay"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Interactive Rebase Basics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What it is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Interactive rebase== opens a todo list of commits in your editor. You label each line with an action, and git replays the commits to match.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git rebase -i HEAD~4",
            "pick a1f3c2e add login form",
            "pick b7d9e10 fix typo",
            "pick c42aa8b add tests",
            "pick d90f5b3 wire up API"
          ],
          "note": "oldest first, newest last"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`HEAD~4` lists the last **4** commits",
            "Oldest sits at the top, the opposite of `git log`",
            "Commits replay **top to bottom**, so order matters"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The six actions",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Action",
            "Effect",
            "Pauses?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`pick`",
              "keep commit unchanged",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`reword`",
              "keep changes, edit message",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`edit`",
              "stop after applying; amend or split",
              "yes"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Action",
            "Effect",
            "Message"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`squash`",
              "meld into previous commit",
              "both combined"
            ],
            [
              "`fixup`",
              "meld into previous commit",
              "this one discarded"
            ],
            [
              "`drop`",
              "delete the commit",
              "gone"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "edit = pause",
          "text": "After `edit`, amend or split, then run `git rebase --continue`. A removed line works like `drop`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Worked example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "pick a1f3c2e add login form",
            "fixup b7d9e10 fix typo",
            "reword c42aa8b add tests",
            "exec npm test",
            "drop d90f5b3 wire up API"
          ],
          "note": "exec runs after the line above"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Line",
            "Action",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "pick",
              "login form kept as is"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "fixup",
              "typo folded into 1, message gone"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "reword",
              "tests commit gets a new message"
            ],
            [
              "4",
              "exec",
              "`npm test` runs; failure pauses"
            ],
            [
              "5",
              "drop",
              "API commit deleted"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Swap two lines and the commits swap places",
            "If both touch the same code, a **conflict** may appear",
            "`exec npm test` checks the build after a commit"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "The todo list"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Todo Edge Cases & Cheatsheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Edge cases",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git rebase -i --root",
            "pick 1e0aa77 initial commit",
            "pick a1f3c2e add login form"
          ],
          "note": "--root rewrites the first commit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reading the todo like `git log`, newest on top",
            "Deleting **every** line: empty todo aborts the rebase",
            "Reordering commits that edit the same lines",
            "Using `squash` on the first line: nothing to meld into"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. exec Checks",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`exec` runs a shell command after the line above it",
            "A non-zero exit **pauses** the rebase at that commit",
            "Fix the code, amend, then `--continue`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "pick a1f3c2e add login form",
            "exec npm test",
            "pick c42aa8b add tests",
            "exec npm test"
          ],
          "note": "tests every commit as it replays"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Todo Cheatsheet",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Key",
            "Short",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`p`",
              "pick",
              "keep as is"
            ],
            [
              "`r`",
              "reword",
              "new message"
            ],
            [
              "`e`",
              "edit",
              "stop to amend"
            ],
            [
              "`s`",
              "squash",
              "meld, keep msgs"
            ],
            [
              "`f`",
              "fixup",
              "meld, drop msg"
            ],
            [
              "`d`",
              "drop",
              "delete commit"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Short forms",
          "text": "Write `p`, `r`, `e`, `s`, `f`, `d` instead of the full word. Git accepts both."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Safe Workflow",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Run `git log --oneline` to pick how far back",
            "Open `git rebase -i HEAD~N` and edit the todo",
            "Save, then resolve any stop that appears",
            "Run `git log --oneline` again to verify"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase --continue  # next step",
            "git rebase --abort     # undo all"
          ],
          "note": "abort restores the old branch"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Reordering",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Move a line up or down to reorder commits",
            "Replay follows the new order, top to bottom",
            "Same-code edits may **conflict** after a swap"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "pick c42aa8b add tests",
            "pick a1f3c2e add login form"
          ],
          "note": "tests now replay first"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Drop Two Ways",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Todo edit",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`drop` word",
              "commit removed"
            ],
            [
              "delete the line",
              "commit removed"
            ],
            [
              "delete all lines",
              "rebase aborts"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Prefer drop",
          "text": "Writing `drop` leaves a visible record in the todo. A deleted line is easy to miss."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Todo is oldest first, replays top to bottom, and an empty todo aborts."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "The todo list"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Squash, Fixup, Reword, Edit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Example Todo List",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "pick a1b2c3 Add login",
            "fixup d4e5f6 typo",
            "squash 7a8b9c tests",
            "reword 0f1e2d msg"
          ],
          "note": "oldest commit first, replays top-down"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Squash a WIP series: keep the ==first pick==",
            "Mark every later WIP commit `squash` or `fixup`",
            "**Reorder** fixes next to their targets first"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Action Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Action",
            "Editor?",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "squash",
              "opens editor",
              "merges both messages"
            ],
            [
              "fixup",
              "silent",
              "keeps earlier message"
            ],
            [
              "reword",
              "message only",
              "code untouched"
            ],
            [
              "edit",
              "stops at commit",
              "amend, then continue"
            ],
            [
              "drop",
              "none",
              "commit removed"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Edit and Split",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# marked edit: rebase stops",
            "git commit --amend",
            "git rebase --continue"
          ],
          "note": "amend only after the stop"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# split: mark the commit edit",
            "git reset HEAD^   # unstage all",
            "git add -p         # pick hunks",
            "git commit -m \"part 1\"",
            "git commit -am \"part 2\"",
            "git rebase --continue"
          ],
          "note": "one commit per logical change"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "__reword__ fixes an old typo, code stays identical",
            "__drop__ removes debug code or a bad experiment",
            "`--amend` = latest commit only; `rebase -i` = older ones"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Using `--amend` on an older commit",
            "Rewriting commits teammates already pulled",
            "Squashing unrelated changes into one blob",
            "Final commit that does not build or pass tests"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Verify",
          "text": "Run `git log --oneline` before AND after the rebase."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Rewrite only ==unpushed== or personal-branch commits",
            "Keep each final commit **atomic**: builds, passes tests",
            "Compare both logs: WIP noise gone, intent kept"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git log --oneline   # before",
            "git rebase -i HEAD~5",
            "git log --oneline   # after"
          ],
          "note": "WIP noise should be gone"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Atomic commits",
          "text": "One logical change per commit, and every commit builds."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Rebase in practice"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Autosquash and fixup! Commits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git commit --fixup=<sha>` makes a commit titled ==fixup! <original subject>==",
            "`git commit --squash=<sha>` makes `squash! <subject>` and lets you edit the message",
            "`--fixup=reword:<sha>` rewords the target on autosquash",
            "`--fixup=amend:<sha>` (an amend! commit) replaces **content and message**"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How autosquash works",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git rebase -i --autosquash` scans for fixup!/squash! subjects",
            "Each one moves ==under its target== in the todo",
            "Its action flips from pick to fixup or squash",
            "It only reorders the todo; you still __review__ it, then save"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tables",
          "spec": {
            "tables": [
              {
                "title": "Before",
                "headers": [
                  "Action",
                  "Commit"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "add login"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "add logout"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "fixup! add login"
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "After autosquash",
                "headers": [
                  "Action",
                  "Commit"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "add login"
                  ],
                  [
                    "fixup",
                    "fixup! add login"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "add logout"
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "arrow": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example workflow",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git commit --fixup=a1b2c3",
            "git rebase -i --autosquash a1b2c3^",
            "# review todo, save, done"
          ],
          "note": "a1b2c3^ keeps the target in range"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR=true \\",
            "  git rebase -i --autosquash \\",
            "  origin/main",
            "git config rebase.autoSquash true"
          ],
          "note": "skips the editor completely"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setup",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`--autosquash origin/main`",
              "everything since main"
            ],
            [
              "`rebase.autoSquash true`",
              "default for `-i`"
            ],
            [
              "`GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR=true`",
              "accept todo as-is"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Workflow",
          "text": "Commit fixes as you review, then autosquash ==once== before merging."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Commit Flavours",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Title made",
            "On autosquash"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`--fixup=<sha>`",
              "fixup! subject",
              "fold, drop msg"
            ],
            [
              "`--squash=<sha>`",
              "squash! subject",
              "fold, edit msg"
            ],
            [
              "`--fixup=reword:`",
              "amend! subject",
              "new message only"
            ],
            [
              "`--fixup=amend:`",
              "amend! subject",
              "new code + message"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git commit --fixup=reword:a1b2c3",
            "git commit --fixup=amend:a1b2c3",
            "git commit --squash=a1b2c3"
          ],
          "note": "pick the flavour you need"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use `fixup!` for a small code fix to an old commit",
            "Use `reword:` when only the message was wrong",
            "Use `amend:` to change both at once"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Match by SHA",
          "text": "`--fixup=<sha>` writes the subject, so a rename breaks it; a title typed as `fixup! <sha>` survives."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Match by subject or SHA",
          "text": "Keep targets in range, keep their subjects unchanged, review the todo."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Fold fixes automatically"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Autosquash Pitfalls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Renaming the target commit **breaks** the subject match",
            "Target outside the rebase range stays a plain commit",
            "Using GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR=true without reading the todo",
            "Assuming autosquash rewrites; it only __reorders__ the todo"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Fixing Each Mistake",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Renamed target",
              "retitle to `fixup! <sha>`"
            ],
            [
              "Target out of range",
              "start at `<sha>^`"
            ],
            [
              "Blind editor skip",
              "read todo first"
            ],
            [
              "Unsure of result",
              "`git log --oneline`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git log --oneline origin/main..",
            "git rebase -i --autosquash \\",
            "  a1b2c3^",
            "git log --oneline"
          ],
          "note": "check range, rebase, verify"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Check the range",
          "text": "Every fixup! needs its target in the rebase range, or it stays a plain commit."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pre-flight Checklist",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Targets are inside the ==rebase range==",
            "Target subjects are unchanged since the fixup",
            "Todo reviewed before saving, even with `GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR`",
            "Only ==unpushed== commits are being rewritten"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Autosquash",
          "text": "It reorders the todo and sets actions. You still review and save."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Fold fixes automatically"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resolving Conflicts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is a Conflict?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each replayed commit is a ==three-way merge==",
            "If both sides touched the same lines, it can't apply cleanly",
            "Rebase **pauses** and prints `CONFLICT (content)`",
            "Files get `<<<<<<<`, `=======`, `>>>>>>>` markers"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Resolve Loop",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# edit files, remove the markers",
            "git add app.js      # mark resolved",
            "git rebase --continue  # next commit",
            "git status          # rebase in progress"
          ],
          "note": "never run git commit mid-conflict"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "--continue",
              "resume with next commit"
            ],
            [
              "--abort",
              "back to pre-rebase state"
            ],
            [
              "--skip",
              "drop current commit"
            ],
            [
              "mergetool",
              "visual 3-way resolver"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Edit mode only",
          "text": "Just add and --continue. Run git commit only when stopped by an edit step."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Ours vs Theirs (Flipped!)",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Label",
            "During rebase",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ours",
              "upstream branch",
              "base you build on"
            ],
            [
              "theirs",
              "your commit",
              "being replayed"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git checkout --theirs app.js",
            "# keeps YOUR replayed commit",
            "git checkout --ours app.js",
            "# keeps the upstream version",
            "git add app.js"
          ],
          "note": "flipped versus merge"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Dry Run: 3/7 Stops",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Step",
            "Status",
            "Action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "2/7",
              "clean",
              "auto-applied"
            ],
            [
              "3/7",
              "CONFLICT",
              "edit, add, --continue"
            ],
            [
              "4/7",
              "same conflict",
              "rerere or repeat fix"
            ],
            [
              "5/7",
              "upstream has it",
              "--skip"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "1",
              "2",
              "3",
              "4",
              "5",
              "6",
              "7"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [
              {
                "index": 2,
                "label": "stopped 3/7",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "index": 6,
                "label": "remaining",
                "ink": "blue"
              }
            ],
            "highlight": [
              2
            ],
            "dim": [
              0,
              1
            ],
            "caption": "git status shows which step you are on"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Running `git commit` instead of **--continue**",
            "Mixing up ours/theirs and keeping the wrong side",
            "Using --skip on a commit that is not upstream",
            "Rebasing 30 commits: ==squash first==, resolve once"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Escape hatch",
          "text": "Lost? `git rebase --abort` restores the branch exactly as before."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "continue, abort, skip"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Moving Branches with --onto",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is --onto?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git rebase --onto <newbase> <oldbase> <branch>`",
            "Replays commits in ==oldbase..branch== on top of newbase",
            "Omit <branch>: rebases the **checked-out** branch",
            "Plain rebase: upstream is cut point AND new base"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three Arguments",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase --onto \\",
            "  main \\      # where to LAND",
            "  feature \\   # where to CUT",
            "  topic       # what to MOVE"
          ],
          "note": "oldbase itself is NOT replayed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Arg",
            "Answers",
            "Role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "newbase",
              "where to land",
              "new parent"
            ],
            [
              "oldbase",
              "where to cut",
              "range start"
            ],
            [
              "branch",
              "what to move",
              "range end"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: Stacked Branch",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "A-B-C",
                "sub": "main",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "D-E",
                "sub": "feature",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "F-G",
                "sub": "topic",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "F'-G' on C",
                "sub": "after",
                "ink": "purple"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git log --graph --oneline --all",
            "git rebase --onto main feature topic",
            "git log --graph --oneline --all"
          ],
          "note": "log before AND after to verify"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "After --onto",
          "text": "`feature` is untouched. Only `topic` moves."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. When to Use It",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parent was ==squash-merged== and diverged from your copy",
            "`git rebase --onto main <old-parent-tip> topic`",
            "`git rebase --onto A B` drops commits between A and B"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Command"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Move stack",
              "`--onto main feature topic`"
            ],
            [
              "After squash",
              "`--onto main <old-tip> topic`"
            ],
            [
              "Cut middle",
              "`--onto A B`"
            ],
            [
              "Plain",
              "`rebase main`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Safety Checks",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Name all **three** arguments so nothing is guessed",
            "Check `oldbase..branch` lists only the commits to move",
            "Expect new SHAs for every moved commit",
            "The old base branch is never rewritten"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git branch backup-topic",
            "git log --oneline feature..topic",
            "git rebase --onto main feature topic"
          ],
          "note": "preview the range, then move"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Branch",
            "Before",
            "After"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "main",
              "A-B-C",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "feature",
              "D-E",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "topic",
              "F-G",
              "F'-G' on C"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Three questions",
          "text": "Where to land, where to cut, what to move. Answer all three."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Transplant a range"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Shared Branches & force-with-lease",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Golden Rule",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Never rebase== commits others already pulled",
            "Rebase makes **new SHAs**, so copies diverge",
            "Personal branch behind a PR: fine, __announce it__ to reviewers"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Who",
            "Holds",
            "SHA"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "origin",
              "old commit",
              "`C`"
            ],
            [
              "Teammate",
              "old commit",
              "`C`"
            ],
            [
              "You (rebased)",
              "new commit",
              "`C'`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Pushing Rewritten History",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase main",
            "git push        # rejected",
            "git push --force-with-lease",
            "# ! [rejected] non-fast-forward"
          ],
          "note": "normal push fails after rebase"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Remote moved?",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`--force`",
              "no / yes",
              "overwrites **blindly**"
            ],
            [
              "`--force-with-lease`",
              "no",
              "push succeeds"
            ],
            [
              "`--force-with-lease`",
              "yes",
              "**fails**, teammate safe"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lease checks remote == your __last fetch__",
            "Pin it: `--force-with-lease=feat:<sha>`",
            "`--force-if-includes`: tip must be merged locally"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git push --force-with-lease=feat:<sha>",
            "git push --force-with-lease \\",
            "  --force-if-includes"
          ],
          "note": "stricter: pin sha plus includes check"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "fetch",
                "sub": "see remote",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "rebase",
                "sub": "local only",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "lease push",
                "sub": "checked",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "verify",
                "sub": "git log",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Safe order",
          "text": "Fetch first, rebase second, lease-push last. Never push blind."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Tell reviewers before you rewrite a PR branch",
            "Ask teammates to push their work first",
            "Use a ==personal== branch name, not a shared one"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git fetch origin",
            "git log origin/feat..feat",
            "git push --force-with-lease"
          ],
          "note": "read what you are about to replace"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plain `--force` can **destroy** teammates' commits",
            "IDE auto-fetch silently defeats the lease",
            "Rebasing `main` or a shared `develop`",
            "Rebasing a PR branch without telling reviewers"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Rewrite without regret"
    }
